  "step_3": "The decision reason prioritizes the lottery with the more favorable (higher) maximum outcome, which is Lottery B (4000 Euros vs. 3000 Euros). The individual explicitly refers to accepting a lower probability in order to 'win more', indicating that the higher maximum outcome was the decisive factor. The individual’s reasoning aligns with the core logic of the decision reason: comparing maximum outcomes and preferring the one with the higher value when minimum outcomes are equal (both 0). The information considered (maximum outcomes) and the justification (preferring a chance at more money) match the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

